
"make" macros to control various optional features:

    NO_AES_WG=1       Disable AES_WG encryption.
    AES_WG_SFX=1      Enable AES_WG encryption in UnZipSFX.
    BINS=[L][M][U]    Binaries build list (alphabetical order):
                       L: object library (libizunzip.a)
                       M: main program (UnZip)
                       U: utility programs (fUnZip, UnZipSFX)
                       Default: MU.
    NO_IZ_BZIP2=1     Disable bzip2 compression.
    BZIP2_SFX=1       Enable bzip2 compression in UnZipSFX.
    LOCAL_UNZIP=opts  Add C compiler options, "opts".
    NO_LZMA=1         Disable LZMA compression.
    LZMA_SFX=1        Enable LZMA compression in UnZipSFX.
    NO_PPMD=1         Disable PPMd compression.
    PPMD_SFX=1        Enable PPMd compression in UnZipSFX.
    PROD=subdir       Build product files in "subdir", not ".".
    NO_TRAD=1         Disable Traditional encryption.
    TRAD_SFX=1        Enable Traditional encryption in UnZipSFX.

Examples:

    Make UnZip programs without LZMA or PPMd compression:
        make -f acorn/GMakefile NO_LZMA=1 NO_PPMD=1

    Make UnZipSFX with AES_WG encryption:
        make -f acorn/GMakefile AES_WG_SFX=1

Use the "clean" target to delete any product files before
building with different options.  (Or, specify an empty
PROD directory.)

After UnZip has been built, use the "dashv" target  to get
an "unzip -v" report from the created UnZip executable.

        make -f acorn/GMakefile [ PROD=subdir ...] dashv

See the files INSTALL, docs.unzip/txt, and acorn.GMakefile for
more information.

